abstract: >-
  Single-file Bash report on an Ubuntu or Debian server: the month's traffic against the
  provider's bandwidth cap with a projection to the end of the month (from vnstat, Munin or the
  kernel counters), memory, swap, load, disks and inodes, services, failed units and pending
  updates, with exit codes that a monitoring system understands and a JSON output. For the disks
  it forecasts when each filesystem will be full from a week of history, names the largest and
  fastest-growing folders, and lists what can be freed safely with the exact command for each
  item; run hourly from cron, it sends a short alert through the Hermes agent or any command only
  when something needs attention.
